  "comment": "The animals tools/bodies/index.mjs builds from nothing (#787, #789). One row per animal. `joints` are { name, parent, head }: a glTF joint name (the hound's where one exists), its parent joint (null for the root) and where it sits in the bind pose, in metres, +x the animal's left, +y up, +z the way it faces. Every joint binds unrotated. `parts` are boxes or prisms, flat-shaded, each rigidly weighted to one joint: { shape, center, size, joint, material }, with `sides` and `axis` on a prism. `materials` are { color } in linear 0..1; a material with `primitive` is drawn inside that one by vertex colour rather than as a primitive of its own, which is how a hide gets patches inside #789's four primitives. `tint` says whether src/npc.js's tintBody multiplies it; the generator does not read it, test/assets.mjs does. `clips` are { name, seconds, cycles, driver, moves }, keyed at 51 uniform times; each move is { bone, axis, rest, amp, phase, rate } and its value at key k of 50 is rest + amp * sin(2 pi (cycles * rate * k / 50 + phase)), in degrees about the axis in the joint's parent frame for `path` rotation (the default) and in metres along it for `path` translation. `rate` is an integer and defaults to 1. Edit a row, run `npm run bodies:render`, commit the .glb with it.",
